@startuml
' Sequence diagram: monitor data edit flow (PUT /monitores/:consignee)
' Covers the pvapi-gmru feature — partial update of monitor name, email, phone, and address

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Estabelecimento (Shop)" as Shop
participant "Auth Middleware" as Auth
participant "Policy Gate\n(ConsigneeGate)" as Gate
participant "Consignee Handler" as Handler
participant "shopmodel\nHasConsignee" as Owns
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Authentication ==

Shop -> Auth: PUT /monitores/:consignee\n(JWT + JSON body)
Auth --> Shop: JWT decoded,\nuser in context

== Authorization Check ==

Handler -> Gate: Dispatch(method=PUT,\nrole=Shop, params)
Gate -> Owns: Owns(shopID, consigneeID)
Owns -> DB: ShopHasConsigneeQuery\n(SELECT ... FROM consignees\nWHERE shop_id=$1 AND id=$2)
DB --> Owns: hasConsignee=true/false
Owns --> Gate: true (owns)
Gate --> Handler: allow

== Partial Update (Atomic Transaction) ==

group pgx.BeginFunc transaction
  note right of Handler: Build dynamic SET map\nwith squirrel.Update().SetMap()
  note right: Only non-nil *string fields\nincluded in the query

  alt has user fields (name, email)
    Handler -> DB: UPDATE users SET name=?, email=?\nWHERE id = (SELECT user_id\nFROM consignees WHERE id=$1)
    DB --> Handler: OK
  end

  alt has phone field
    Handler -> DB: UPDATE consignees\nSET telephone = ?\nWHERE id = $1
    DB --> Handler: OK
  end

  alt has address fields (street, number, etc.)
    Handler -> DB: UPDATE addresses\nSET street=?, number=?, ...\nWHERE id = (SELECT address_id\nFROM consignees WHERE id=$1)
    DB --> Handler: OK
  end
end

== Retrieve Updated Resource ==

Handler -> DB: SELECT FROM\nconsignees_info_full_view\nWHERE consignee_id = $1
DB --> Handler: full ConsigneeResource
Handler --> Shop: 200 OK\n{ "monitor": { ... } }

note right of Shop: Returns complete monitor\nwith all fields — unchanged\nfields show old values

@enduml
